  "bodyText": "Home\nVisit Us\nExhibitions\nEvents\nOnline Talks\nOxfordshire’s Military Heritage in 50 Objects\nCollections\nBlog\nResearch\nLearning\nShop\nCart\nMy Account\nAbout\nBecome a Friend\nSupport Us\nRoom Hire\n\n01993 810 210\n\nfrontofhouse@sofo.org.uk\n\n  \nHome\nEvents\nExhibitions\nCollections\nFriends’ Membership\nVisit\nShop\nBasket\nMy Account\nOxfordshire’s Military Heritage in 50 Objects\nResearch\nLearning\nOnline Talks\nBlog\nSupport Us\nRoom Hire\nImage Services\nAbout\nBooks\nGifts\nGliderborne: The Story of 2nd Battalion The Oxfordshire and Buckinghamshire Light Infantry (The 52nd) in WWII\n£28.00\n\nGliderborne: The Story of 2nd Battalion The Oxfordshire and Buckinghamshire Light Infantry (The 52nd) in WWII quantity\nAdd to Cart\n\nThe history of the Ox & Bucks Light Infantry's 2nd Battalion during the Second World War, including the famous Pegasus Bridge operation. Each copy is signed by Michael Massy-Beresford, the author.\n\nContents:\n\nDedication\n\nCompiler's Note\n\nChapter One: The 52nd's Return from India\n\nChapter Two: The 52nd July 1940 - October 1941 Training in the UK\n\nChapter Three: Aerial Precursors and the Axis Airborne Operations of 1940/41\n\nChapter Four: Early Allied Airborne Operations 1940 - 1943\n\nChapter Five: The 52nd Trains for Airborne Duties Oct 1941 - March 1943\n\nChapter Six: The 52nd in the UK, April 1943 - May 1944\n\nChapter Seven: Normandy 1944\n\nChapter Eight: Captain Priday's Account of Events 6th/7th June 1944\n\nChapter Nine: The Arnhem Operation and the Divisional Defence Platoon\n\nChapter Ten: The Dash to the Ardennes, December 1944\n\nChapter Eleven: Rhine Crossing March 1945\n\nChapter Twelve: The Advance to the Baltic\n\nChapter Thirteen: Operation 'Canloan'\n\nChapter Fourteen: The 52nd in India and Palestine 1945 - 48\n\nEpilogue\n\nRoll of Honour\n\nObituaries\n\nCompiler's Final Note\n\nApendices\n\nRelated products\nRedcoats to Riflemen: A Short History of the Oxfordshire and Buckinghamshire County Regiment\n£4.50 Add to cart\nBugle & Sabre VII\n£5.00 Add to cart\nBugle & Sabre VI\n£5.00 Read more\nRemembered: The Men on the War Memorials of Witney, Crawley and Hailey. Volume 2: 1939-1945.\n£9.99 Add to cart\n\nSoldiers of Oxfordshire Museum\nPark Street.\nWoodstock\nOxfordshire OX20 1SN\n\nPhone and Email:\nGeneral Enquiries & Event Tickets: 01993 810 211\nfrontofhouse@sofo.org.uk\n\nPrivacy Policy\nTerms and conditions",
